A||N||8||87FieroGT||White smoke puff from exhaust?||||8
Z||000000||87FieroGT||10-12-1999||10:44 PM||||I haev been noticing a little puff of white smoke coming from the exhaust when it is first started. I need to know if this means that the rings are wearing out or if it is the seals? The car has a little over 70K original miles on it. Is this something to really worry about or can I go another 30K with it like this.||||reg||8
Z||000001||HotFieroGT||10-12-1999||11:00 PM||||General rule of thumb is: blue smoke means rings or valves, black smoke is fuel (rich).  It sounds like you just may have a little condensation in the exhaust system and as you warm up the car it should disappear.  Just to be safe make sure you haven't blown an intake gasket (common on 60 degree v-6's) by checking the oil and making sure it doesn't have water in it (the oil kind of gets white and milky).  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||10-13-1999||12:48 AM||||With only 70k on an 87 engine, I might suspect valve seals. Does it puff smoke on shifts? Does the puff at startup last only a few seconds? If so, seals. You can replace them if you want. If it is the seals, I'd leave it alone for now if it clears up quickly after start up.<P>Could be the moisture in the exhuast if it lasts more than 1 minute or so. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||87FieroGT||10-13-1999||10:24 PM||||The puff only last on startups and it is white. So I guess I won't worry about it for now. Thanks for the advice.||||reg||12
Z||000004||WisconsinGT||10-13-1999||11:01 PM||||Your problem could also be caused by cracked heads. I had a problem similar to what you describe. It turned out to be two cracked heads.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Racer 1||10-14-1999||03:13 AM||||I would say a water leak into the head. Check your spark plugs before starting the car up in the morning. Also you can stick a small rope down in each cyld and see if theres antifreeze in the combustion chamber.||||reg||9
Z||000006||fieroshop||10-14-1999||10:06 AM||||Some cars have a puff of white smoke when they are first started.My 88 has 124K on it and it still runs good with very high compression readings. My wife' 86 does the same thing and her GT has only 58K on it. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||fotofrank||10-14-1999||05:34 PM||||I too get some white smoke at start-up.<BR>This seems to happen after the car sits for over 8 hours.I also have traces of oil in me air cleaner. The car is an '84 es 4cylendar with 116+ thousand miles on it. I beleave my problem is "blow-by" but I don't know if the correct fix is valves ,rings or a complete rebuild.If u i use an oil aditive the "blow-by" stops but may still "burn" oil.Ant sugestions?||||reg||11
Z||000008||fotofrank||10-14-1999||06:05 PM||||I,too have a puff of white smoak.It usually happens after the car is parked for a while.I also have oil in me air cleaner. This I beleave is called "blow-by". The car is an '84 SE 4 cylender with 116000 miles on it. is the "blow-by" caused by the valves,ringe,gaskets or is a complete rebuild in store for me?||||reg||11
